+{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b7dcef0334c6aa97","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-4-8","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_orig_mnqwy3c7myydayldme4gmzlggrstembxguzggnrwhe4giyy","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# Plan: Reactive Spreadsheet Engine\n\n## Context\nWe need to build a reactive spreadsheet engine as a TypeScript library in `/workspace`. The workspace already has `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `vitest.config.ts`, and ESLint configured, plus an empty `src/`. The task is greenfield: implement storage, formula parsing/evaluation, dependency tracking, reactive recomputation, and circular reference detection, and export a `Spreadsheet` class from `src/index.ts`.\n\n## Goal\nCreate a correctly typed TypeScript library that satisfies the required API and passes comprehensive Vitest tests covering formulas, functions, ranges, reactive updates, circular references, and edge cases.\n\n## Architecture\n\n### File Layout\n- `src/index.ts` — public API: export `Spreadsheet`, plus minimal public types if useful.\n- `src/spreadsheet.ts` — `Spreadsheet` class implementation (storage, API methods, recompute orchestration).\n- `src/parser.ts` — tokenizer and recursive-descent parser for formulas, returning an AST.\n- `src/evaluator.ts` — AST evaluator plus built-in functions and range expansion.\n- `src/refs.ts` — reference utilities (e.g., parse \"A1\"/\"AA1\", column letter <-> number conversion, range expansion).\n- `src/types.ts` — shared types: `CellValue`, `ComputedValue`, `Formula`, AST nodes, etc.\n- `src/index.test.ts` — Vitest unit tests for parser, evaluator, and Spreadsheet API.\n\n### Types\n```typescript\ntype Primitive = string | number | boolean;\ntype CellValue = Primitive | Formula;\ninterface Formula { raw: string; ast: Expr }\n\ntype Expr =\n  | { type: 'literal'; value: Primitive }\n  | { type: 'ref'; cell: string }\n  | { type: 'binary'; op: string; left: Expr; right: Expr }\n  | { type: 'unary'; op: string; expr: Expr }\n  | { type: 'call'; name: string; args: Expr[] }\n  | { type: 'range'; start: string; end: string };\n```\n\n### Core Approach\n1. **Storage**: A `Map<string, CellValue>` keyed by normalized uppercase references. A separate `Map<string, Set<string>>` stores reverse dependencies: `cell -> cells that depend on it`.\n2. **Parsing**: When `set(cell, rawFormula)` is called and the value is a string beginning with `=`, tokenize and parse into AST. Cell references and ranges are normalized to uppercase.\n3. **Dependencies**: Each parsed formula AST is walked to collect direct references (`A1`) and range cells (`A1:A5`) to build `deps(formula)`.\n4. **Compute**: On set, store the raw/formula value, update forward dependency information, detect cycles with a DFS traversing the dependency graph, then recompute the changed cell and all reverse dependents in dependency order (topological evaluation or repeated updates via BFS/DFS).\n5. **Caching**: Store computed values in another `Map<string, ComputedValue>`. Empty cells return `null`. Recompute only affected cells.\n6. **Display**: `getDisplay` coerces the computed value to string (numbers/booleans as `String(value)`, strings as themselves).\n\n### Parsing & Evaluation Details\n- **Tokenizer**: produce tokens for numbers, strings in double quotes, identifiers, cell references, comparison operators, punctuation.\n- **Parser grammar** (precedence low→high):\n  - `expr` -> `comparison`\n  - `comparison` -> `addition ( ( = | <> | > | < | >= | <= ) addition )?`\n  - `addition` -> `multiplication ( (+|-) multiplication )*`\n  - `multiplication` -> `unary ( (*|/) unary )*`\n  - `unary` -> `(+|-)? primary`\n  - `primary` -> number | string literal | boolean literal | cell ref | function call | range | '(' expr ')'\n- **Functions**:\n  - `SUM`, `AVERAGE`, `MIN`, `MAX`, `COUNT` accept a single range argument. Expand ranges to all cell refs; ignore non-numeric cells.\n  - `IF(condition, trueValue, falseValue)` evaluates condition truthiness.\n- **Range expansion**: Given `start:end`, iterate rectangle columns from start col to end col and rows from start row to end row; return cell refs in row-major order.\n- **Operators**: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`; comparison operators return boolean. `=` in formulas is equality (not assignment). Numeric operations coerce operands to numbers when possible.\n- **Errors**: division by zero returns an error value (throw or sentinel?). For this implementation, throw an `EvalError` during evaluation and surface as the computed value; tests will assert thrown behavior only for circular refs per spec. We can represent runtime formula errors as thrown `Error`; the spec does not require error cell values.\n\n### Dependency Tracking & Reactivity\n- `deps(cell)` returns all cells the formula directly depends on.\n- `dependents(cell)` map is updated on every `set`.\n- **Cycle detection**: When setting a formula, before committing, run a DFS from the set cell following dependencies. If any path returns to itself, throw a circular-reference `Error`.\n- **Recompute strategy**: Compute values using a post-order DFS over the dependency graph starting from the changed cell. Ensure each dependency is computed before its dependents, with memoization in the traversal. Because formulas already reference cells that are computed, a simple recursive evaluate with memo also works, but for efficiency and correctness we will compute affected cells in topological order.\n\n### Circular Reference Detection\n- On every `set`, build the dependency graph edge from the cell to its direct deps.\n- Using DFS with color marking (white/gray/black), detect a back edge that forms a cycle involving the cell being set, and throw.\n- This catches direct and indirect cycles.\n\n## Edge Cases to Test\n- Cell references case-insensitively normalized (`a1`, `A1`).\n- Empty cells return `null` and display `''`.\n- Non-numeric cells in `SUM`/`AVERAGE`/`MIN`/`MAX`/`COUNT` are skipped (COUNT counts numeric values only).\n- String literals inside formulas: `=\"hello\"` returns `\"hello\"`.\n- Boolean literals and comparisons: `=IF(A1>10,\"big\",\"small\")`.\n- Large column names (`AA1`, `ZZ1`, `AAA1`).\n- Row and block ranges (`A1:C1`, `A1:C3`).\n- Division by zero throws.\n- Circular references of various depths throw.\n- Removing a formula by setting a raw value clears dependents appropriately.\n- `getCells()` returns all non-empty cells.\n\n## Verification\n1. Run `npm install` to install dependencies.\n2. Run `npm run test` (vitest run). All tests should pass.\n3. Run `npm run build` to ensure TypeScript compiles cleanly.\n4. Run `npm run lint` to ensure no lint errors.\n5. Optionally run `npx tsx src/index.ts` with a small sample script to exercise the API manually.\n\n## Files to Create/Modify\n- `src/index.ts` (create)\n- `src/spreadsheet.ts` (create)\n- `src/parser.ts` (create)\n- `src/evaluator.ts` (create)\n- `src/refs.ts` (create)\n- `src/types.ts` (create)\n- `src/index.test.ts` (create)\n- Delete empty `src/.gitkeep` (optional)\n","planFilePath":"/home/node/.claude/plans/sleepy-coalescing-kay.md"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28327,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b115ed7-b8ae-4188-8167-e3aebba83e63","uuid":"64e74419-8a49-44cc-a366-bb9052636a32"}
