tion in the traversal. Because formulas already reference cells that are computed, a simple recursive evaluate with memo also works, but for efficiency and correctness we will compute affected cells in topological order.\n\n### Circular Reference Detection\n- On every `set`, build the dependency graph edge from the cell to its direct deps.\n- Using DFS with color marking (white/gray/black), detect a back edge that forms a cycle involving the cell being set, and throw.\n- This catches direct and indirect cycles.\n\n## Edge Cases to Test\n- Cell references case-insensitively normalized (`a1`, `A1`).\n- Empty cells return `null` and display `''`.\n- Non-numeric cells in `SUM`/`AVERAGE`/`MIN`/`MAX`/`COUNT` are skipped (COUNT counts numeric values only).\n- String literals inside formulas: `=\"hello\"` returns `\"hello\"`.\n- Boolean literals and comparisons: `=IF(A1>10,\"big\",\"small\")`.\n- Large column names (`AA1`, `ZZ1`, `AAA1`).\n- Row and block ranges (`A1:C1`, `A1:C3`).\n- Division by zero throws.\n- Circular references of various depths throw.\n- Removing a formula by setting a raw value clears dependents appropriately.\n- `getCells()` returns all non-empty cells.\n\n## Verification\n1. Run `npm install` to install dependencies.\n2. Run `npm run test` (vitest run). All tests should pass.\n3. Run `npm run build` to ensure TypeScript compiles cleanly.\n4. Run `npm run lint` to ensure no lint errors.\n5. Optionally run `npx tsx src/index.ts` with a small sample script to exercise the API manually.\n\n## Files to Create/Modify\n- `src/index.ts` (create)\n- `src/spreadsheet.ts` (create)\n- `src/parser.ts` (create)\n- `src/evaluator.ts` (create)\n- `src/refs.ts` (create)\n- `src/types.ts` (create)\n- `src/index.test.ts` (create)\n- Delete empty `src/.gitkeep` (optional)\n","planFilePath":"/home/node/.claude/plans/sleepy-coalescing-kay.md"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"390a1b87-932b-427f-8751-d4807a38e4b0"}
